 ### Verlet Integration
-A numerical integration method for particle dynamics that is time-reversible and unconditionally stable [S4, unofficial]. It updates particle positions based on current and previous positions without explicitly storing velocity [S4, unofficial]. The position is updated using the scheme: $new\_pos = pos + (pos - old\_pos) \cdot damping + acc \cdot dt^2$, followed by updating $old\_pos = pos$ and resetting acceleration [S4, unofficial]. A damping scalar (default 0.99) simulates energy loss [S4, unofficial]. Pinned particles do not update their position or apply forces [S4, unofficial].
+A numerical integration method for particle dynamics that is time-reversible and unconditionally stable [S5, unofficial]. It updates particle positions based on current and previous positions without explicitly storing velocity [S5, unofficial]. The position is updated using the scheme: $new\_pos = pos + (pos - old\_pos) \cdot damping + acc \cdot dt^2$, followed by updating $old\_pos = pos$ and resetting acceleration [S5, unofficial]. A damping scalar (default 0.99) simulates energy loss [S5, unofficial]. Pinned particles do not update their position or apply forces [S5, unofficial].
 
